 # Existing JSON utility
 
-Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin. Existing action: ids. Domain functions accept the payload object; api.dispatch routes it. CLI reports ValueError/KeyError with stderr and exit 2.
+Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin. Domain functions accept the payload object; api.dispatch routes it. CLI reports ValueError/KeyError with stderr and exit 2.
+
+## Actions
+
+### ids
+Payload `{"action":"ids","items":[{"id":...},...]}` → list of ids.
+
+### group
+Payload `{"action":"group","requested":["a","b",...],"responses":[{"id":"a","ok":true,"value":<JSON>},{"id":"b","ok":false,"error":"..."}]}`
+
+- `requested`: unique string ids in desired order. `responses`: at most one response per requested id.
+- Returns `{"successes":[{"id":...,"value":...}],"failures":[{"id":...,"error":"..."}],"missing":["..."]}`; every array follows requested order regardless of response arrival order. Missing ids appear only in `missing`; falsey successful values (`null`, `false`, `0`, `""`) stay in `successes`. Nothing is retried or synthesized.
+- `ValueError` (CLI: exit 2, message on stderr) on duplicate requested ids, a response id not in `requested`, or duplicate responses for one id.
+
+Input payloads are never mutated, including rejected ones.
+
+```
+echo '{"action":"group","requested":["c","a","b"],"responses":[{"id":"a","ok":true,"value":0},{"id":"c","ok":false,"error":"boom"}]}' | python cli.py
+{"successes": [{"id": "a", "value": 0}], "failures": [{"id": "c", "error": "boom"}], "missing": ["b"]}
+```
+
+Regression tests: `python -B tests/test_group.py`.
